/* =====================================================================
   DAASI-3640 | 30: the comp text that is missing from the fact, added
   by one UPDATE.

   Rev 2 (11/11, evening): the run is narrowed. Rev 1 changed every comp
   whose text differs from the v1.14 rules, 7.9 million of them. From
   the review with Pete on 11/11: that is too many, only the rows that
   need it are to change, and a comment is not to be replaced with
   nothing. Rev 1 is kept in archive_v1.14/.

   What the 7.9 million are. Two kinds of comp:
     text missing     The remarks (CMS's second note field, which the
                      load never read) and comments typed in CMS after
                      the comp was loaded. Expected: 1.2 to 1.3 million.
     text to remove   A note that was written on another comp. CMS
                      reuses comp numbers and the old load matched notes
                      by number alone, so the v1.14 rule gives these
                      comps no such note. Expected: about 6.6 million.
   This run does the first kind only. It writes a text only where the
   comp's own text has a line the fact does not hold today, and it never
   blanks a comment. Part S builds the list of those comps, gives the
   exact count (S2) and shows what it is made of (S3).

   What it leaves. The comps of the second kind keep the note they show
   today. The v1.14 load takes such a note away by itself the next time
   it loads the comp (a change in CMS, or CMS's own purge of the comp
   at 100 days), so the notes that stay for good are those on comps CMS
   has already purged. Taking them out of history is a decision for
   Pete and Tracy: her sample of 11/10 showed them removed. Also not in
   this run, as in rev 1: the comps CMS deleted stay active, host names
   are not refreshed, and the purge-list rows (23) are not needed.

   The streams. Two streams on the fact feed trips
   (COMP_DETAIL_FACT_COMP_DOMAIN_STREAM and ..._FP_DOMAIN_STREAM). The
   UPDATE puts every row it changes into both, and trips has no use for
   a comment. So the order is Pete's: trips drains the streams first,
   then the UPDATE, then the streams are emptied (or recreated), and
   only then is the load resumed. Emptied before the resume, the streams
   lose nothing real: the load is suspended, so the UPDATE is the only
   thing in them. Trips reprocesses none of the rows.

   The window, in order. The load stays suspended from 1 to 8.
     1  Pete   the load task suspended, no run executing
     2  Pete   trips has drained both streams, and TRIP_ROOT_TASK will
               not fire again before step 6 (suspended for the window)
     3  Chris  part A; B1 (the backup, taken now); B2 only if there is
               no key yet; S1 and S2 (the list and its count)
     4  Pete   30b step 1: the count, which must equal S2's
               ROWS_THIS_RUN_UPDATES
     5  Pete   30b step 2: the UPDATE
     6  Pete   30b step 3: the two streams emptied
     7  Chris  part C: the checks. All of them before the resume.
     8  Pete   the load task and TRIP_ROOT_TASK resumed
   For the number alone, ahead of the window: S1, S2 and S3 can be run
   at any time. They read the fact and write one work table. S1 is then
   run again inside the window, so that the list is of that moment.
   Parts A, B, S and C read, or write only to DAAS_TEMP_WORK, and run as
   DAAS_TEAM. Use a Large for B2, S1 and C2.

   Names. Every object is written with its database. For a rehearsal
   in UAT, replace DAAS_PROD. with DAAS_UAT. throughout, in this file
   and in 30b. If PROD work tables are kept somewhere other than
   DAAS_PROD.DAAS_TEMP_WORK, replace that one name throughout, in both.

   Part S and the UPDATE have not run on Snowflake yet, so the rehearsal
   in UAT comes first.
   ===================================================================== */


/* ---------------------------------------------------------------------
   A. BEFORE (read-only)
   --------------------------------------------------------------------- */

-- A1. The deploy is in: the fact has the remarks column (1).
SELECT COUNT(*) AS has_column
FROM DAAS_PROD.INFORMATION_SCHEMA.COLUMNS
WHERE TABLE_SCHEMA = 'DAAS_CORE' AND TABLE_NAME = 'COMP_DETAIL_FACT' AND COLUMN_NAME = 'COMMENTS_EXTENDED';

-- A2. The load is suspended: "state" reads suspended. (No row means this role cannot see the
--     task, and Pete confirms it.)
SHOW TASKS LIKE 'RAW2CORE_HETCMS_COMP_DETAIL_FACT_TASK' IN SCHEMA DAAS_PROD.DAAS_COMMON;

-- A3. Trips has drained both streams: 0 and 0. A SELECT does not consume a stream.
SELECT 'COMP_DOMAIN' AS STREAM, COUNT(*) AS ROWS_WAITING
FROM DAAS_PROD.DAAS_CORE.COMP_DETAIL_FACT_COMP_DOMAIN_STREAM
UNION ALL
SELECT 'FP_DOMAIN', COUNT(*)
FROM DAAS_PROD.DAAS_CORE.COMP_DETAIL_FACT_FP_DOMAIN_STREAM;


/* ---------------------------------------------------------------------
   B. BACKUP AND ANSWER KEY (nothing in the fact changes yet)
   --------------------------------------------------------------------- */

-- B1. Zero-copy backup of the fact, taken inside the window with the load suspended, so that it
--     is the fact exactly as the UPDATE finds it. Plain CREATE, so a rerun cannot overwrite it.
--     Keep it for 90 days.
--     If it answers "already exists", a backup from an earlier sitting is there, and it is out
--     of date as soon as the load has run since. While 30b has not run it protects nothing, so
--     drop it and take it again:
--       DROP TABLE DAAS_PROD.DAAS_TEMP_WORK.COMP_DETAIL_FACT_BKP_DAASI3640_UPD;
--     Never after 30b has run: from then on it is the only copy of the text as it was.
CREATE TABLE DAAS_PROD.DAAS_TEMP_WORK.COMP_DETAIL_FACT_BKP_DAASI3640_UPD
  CLONE DAAS_PROD.DAAS_CORE.COMP_DETAIL_FACT;

--     The backup is the fact of this moment: two rows, the same two values.
SELECT '1. the fact' AS what, COUNT(*) AS rows_, MAX(UPDATED_DTTM) AS last_change
FROM DAAS_PROD.DAAS_CORE.COMP_DETAIL_FACT
UNION ALL
SELECT '2. the backup', COUNT(*), MAX(UPDATED_DTTM)
FROM DAAS_PROD.DAAS_TEMP_WORK.COMP_DETAIL_FACT_BKP_DAASI3640_UPD;

-- B2. The answer key: for every active HETCMS comp, the comment and remarks the fact holds now
--     (OLD_) and the ones the v1.14 rules give (NEW_), with the row's own key
--     (COMP_DETAIL_FACT_SK). The statement is rev 1's, unchanged. Reads the bridge (251M rows):
--     use a Large.
--     A key built at an earlier sitting can stay. S1 leaves out every row the load has rewritten
--     since, and those rows already read as the rules say. Build it again if it is more than a
--     few days old.
CREATE OR REPLACE TRANSIENT TABLE DAAS_PROD.DAAS_TEMP_WORK.DAASI3640_UPD_KEY AS
WITH comps AS (
    SELECT COMP_DETAIL_FACT_SK, COMP_NBR, ISHDRW, PROPERTY_CD, CASINO_OUTLET_CD, GUEST_ID, ISSUE_DT,
           COMP_COMMENTS_DESC AS OLD_COMMENT,
           COMMENTS_EXTENDED  AS OLD_REMARKS,
           UPDATED_DTTM       AS OLD_UPDATED_DTTM,
           BATCH_ID           AS OLD_BATCH_ID,
           MD5_CHECKSUM       AS OLD_MD5
    FROM DAAS_PROD.DAAS_CORE.COMP_DETAIL_FACT
    WHERE DELETE_IND = 'N'
      AND SOURCE_SYSTEM_NM = 'HETCMS'
),
comments AS (   -- v1.14 rule: own lines (the line's guest held the comp), plus bridged lines: for a
                -- comp the feed first saw after its issue date, a line whose guest never held any
                -- comp on that number, written by the same person (same primary account in the
                -- bridge) and not older than the comp. The holder's own line wins on a line number.
    SELECT CNUMRW, ISHDRW, PROPERTY_CODE,
           LISTAGG(CMNTCM, '|') WITHIN GROUP (ORDER BY CSEQCM) AS CMNTCM
    FROM (
        SELECT CNUMRW, ISHDRW, PROPERTY_CODE, CSEQCM, CMNTCM
        FROM (
            SELECT H.CNUMRW, H.ISHDRW, H.PROPERTY_CODE, L.CSEQCM, L.CMNTCM, 1 AS MATCH_RANK,
                   L.OPERATION_DATE, L.OPERATION_SEQUENCE_NBR, L.CREATED_DATE
            FROM (SELECT DISTINCT CNUMRW, ISHDRW, PROPERTY_CODE, SYIDRW
                  FROM DAAS_PROD.DAAS_RAW_HETCMS.CMPRW_RAW) H
            JOIN (SELECT SYIDCM, "CMP#CM", CSEQCM, CMNTCM, PROPERTY_CODE,
                         OPERATION_DATE, OPERATION_SEQUENCE_NBR, CREATED_DATE
                  FROM DAAS_PROD.DAAS_RAW_HETCMS.ECPCMPCM_RAW
                  QUALIFY ROW_NUMBER() OVER (PARTITION BY SYIDCM, "CMP#CM", CSEQCM, PROPERTY_CODE
                          ORDER BY OPERATION_DATE DESC, OPERATION_SEQUENCE_NBR DESC, CREATED_DATE DESC) = 1) L
              ON L.SYIDCM = H.SYIDRW AND L."CMP#CM" = H.CNUMRW AND L.PROPERTY_CODE = H.PROPERTY_CODE
            UNION ALL
            SELECT H.CNUMRW, H.ISHDRW, H.PROPERTY_CODE, L.CSEQCM, L.CMNTCM, 2 AS MATCH_RANK,
                   L.OPERATION_DATE, L.OPERATION_SEQUENCE_NBR, L.CREATED_DATE
            FROM (SELECT SYIDCM, "CMP#CM", CSEQCM, CMNTCM, PROPERTY_CODE,
                         OPERATION_DATE, OPERATION_SEQUENCE_NBR, CREATED_DATE,
                         MIN(OPERATION_DATE) OVER (PARTITION BY SYIDCM, "CMP#CM", CSEQCM, PROPERTY_CODE) AS FIRST_SEEN
                  FROM DAAS_PROD.DAAS_RAW_HETCMS.ECPCMPCM_RAW
                  QUALIFY ROW_NUMBER() OVER (PARTITION BY SYIDCM, "CMP#CM", CSEQCM, PROPERTY_CODE
                          ORDER BY OPERATION_DATE DESC, OPERATION_SEQUENCE_NBR DESC, CREATED_DATE DESC) = 1) L
            JOIN (SELECT CNUMRW, ISHDRW, PROPERTY_CODE, SYIDRW
                  FROM (SELECT CNUMRW, ISHDRW, PROPERTY_CODE, SYIDRW,
                               MIN(OPERATION_DATE) OVER (PARTITION BY CNUMRW, ISHDRW, PROPERTY_CODE) AS FIRST_SEEN
                        FROM DAAS_PROD.DAAS_RAW_HETCMS.CMPRW_RAW)
                  WHERE FIRST_SEEN::DATE > DATEADD(DAY, 1, DECODE(ISHDRW, 0, '1899-12-31'::DATE, ISHDRW + '1899-12-31'::DATE))
                  GROUP BY CNUMRW, ISHDRW, PROPERTY_CODE, SYIDRW) H
              ON L."CMP#CM" = H.CNUMRW AND L.PROPERTY_CODE = H.PROPERTY_CODE
            JOIN (SELECT PROPERTY_CD, MIN(PROPERTY_ID)::VARCHAR AS PROPERTY_ID
                  FROM DAAS_PROD.DAAS_CORE.PROPERTY_DIM GROUP BY PROPERTY_CD) P
              ON P.PROPERTY_CD = H.PROPERTY_CODE
            JOIN DAAS_PROD.DAAS_CORE.GUEST_XREF_BRIDGE_LKP BL
              ON BL.XREF_ACCOUNT_NBR = P.PROPERTY_ID || LPAD(L.SYIDCM::VARCHAR, 8, '0')
            JOIN DAAS_PROD.DAAS_CORE.GUEST_XREF_BRIDGE_LKP BH
              ON BH.XREF_ACCOUNT_NBR = P.PROPERTY_ID || LPAD(H.SYIDRW::VARCHAR, 8, '0')
             AND BH.PRIMARY_ACCOUNT_NBR = BL.PRIMARY_ACCOUNT_NBR
            WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM DAAS_PROD.DAAS_RAW_HETCMS.CMPRW_RAW N
                              WHERE N.CNUMRW = L."CMP#CM" AND N.PROPERTY_CODE = L.PROPERTY_CODE AND N.SYIDRW = L.SYIDCM)
              AND L.FIRST_SEEN::DATE >= DATEADD(DAY, -1, DECODE(H.ISHDRW, 0, '1899-12-31'::DATE, H.ISHDRW + '1899-12-31'::DATE))
        )
        QUALIFY ROW_NUMBER() OVER (PARTITION BY CNUMRW, ISHDRW, PROPERTY_CODE, CSEQCM
                ORDER BY MATCH_RANK, OPERATION_DATE DESC, OPERATION_SEQUENCE_NBR DESC, CREATED_DATE DESC) = 1
    )
    GROUP BY CNUMRW, ISHDRW, PROPERTY_CODE
),
remarks AS (    -- remarks rule: a remark line belongs to the comp live on its number when written
    SELECT CNUMRW, ISHDRW, PROPERTY_CODE,
           LEFT(LISTAGG(EXPLRM, '|') WITHIN GROUP (ORDER BY SEQNRM), 4000) AS COMMENTS_EXTENDED
    FROM (
        SELECT C.CNUMRW, C.ISHDRW, C.PROPERTY_CODE, R.SEQNRM, R.EXPLRM
        FROM (SELECT CNUMRW, ISHDRW, PROPERTY_CODE, FIRST_SEEN,
                     LAG(FIRST_SEEN)  OVER (PARTITION BY CNUMRW, PROPERTY_CODE ORDER BY FIRST_SEEN, ISHDRW) AS PREV_FIRST_SEEN,
                     LEAD(FIRST_SEEN) OVER (PARTITION BY CNUMRW, PROPERTY_CODE ORDER BY FIRST_SEEN, ISHDRW) AS NEXT_FIRST_SEEN
              FROM (SELECT CNUMRW, ISHDRW, PROPERTY_CODE, MIN(OPERATION_DATE) AS FIRST_SEEN
                    FROM DAAS_PROD.DAAS_RAW_HETCMS.CMPRW_RAW
                    GROUP BY CNUMRW, ISHDRW, PROPERTY_CODE)) C
        JOIN DAAS_PROD.DAAS_RAW_HETCMS.CMPRM_RAW R
          ON R.CNUMRM = C.CNUMRW
         AND R.PROPERTY_CODE = C.PROPERTY_CODE
         AND (C.PREV_FIRST_SEEN IS NULL OR R.OPERATION_DATE >= DATEADD(SECOND, -60, C.FIRST_SEEN))
         AND (C.NEXT_FIRST_SEEN IS NULL OR R.OPERATION_DATE <  DATEADD(SECOND, -60, C.NEXT_FIRST_SEEN))
        QUALIFY ROW_NUMBER() OVER (PARTITION BY C.CNUMRW, C.ISHDRW, C.PROPERTY_CODE, R.SEQNRM
                ORDER BY R.OPERATION_DATE DESC, R.OPERATION_SEQUENCE_NBR DESC, R.CREATED_DATE DESC) = 1
    )
    GROUP BY CNUMRW, ISHDRW, PROPERTY_CODE
)
SELECT s.*,
       c.CMNTCM            AS NEW_COMMENT,
       r.COMMENTS_EXTENDED AS NEW_REMARKS,
       (c.CMNTCM IS DISTINCT FROM s.OLD_COMMENT OR r.COMMENTS_EXTENDED IS DISTINCT FROM s.OLD_REMARKS) AS WILL_CHANGE
FROM comps s
LEFT JOIN comments c ON c.CNUMRW = s.COMP_NBR AND c.ISHDRW = s.ISHDRW AND c.PROPERTY_CODE = s.PROPERTY_CD
LEFT JOIN remarks  r ON r.CNUMRW = s.COMP_NBR AND r.ISHDRW = s.ISHDRW AND r.PROPERTY_CODE = s.PROPERTY_CD;

-- B3. Everything that differs, for reference: the comps rev 1 would have changed
--     (COMPS_THAT_DIFFER, about 7.9 million on 11/11). The count of this run is S2's.
SELECT COUNT(*)                                                               AS active_comps,
       COUNT_IF(WILL_CHANGE)                                                  AS comps_that_differ,
       COUNT_IF(NEW_COMMENT IS NULL     AND OLD_COMMENT IS NOT NULL)          AS rule_gives_no_comment,
       COUNT_IF(NEW_COMMENT IS NOT NULL AND OLD_COMMENT IS NOT NULL
                AND NEW_COMMENT <> OLD_COMMENT)                               AS rule_gives_another_comment,
       COUNT_IF(NEW_COMMENT IS NOT NULL AND OLD_COMMENT IS NULL)              AS comment_to_add,
       COUNT_IF(NEW_REMARKS IS NOT NULL)                                      AS comps_with_remarks
FROM DAAS_PROD.DAAS_TEMP_WORK.DAASI3640_UPD_KEY;

-- B4. Only if the load has already run under v1.14 since the deploy: the comps it has written,
--     against the answer key. Every remark in the fact was written by v1.14 (the column arrived
--     with it), so the earliest row carrying one marks its first load. Both DIFFER counts should
--     be 0 or a handful. It shows the load and the key agree, so a comp the load touches later
--     gets the same text this UPDATE gives it. All zeros means the load has not run under v1.14
--     yet.
SELECT MIN(t.FIRST_V114_ROW)                                    AS first_v114_row,
       COUNT(e.COMP_NBR)                                        AS comps_loaded_by_v114,
       COUNT_IF(e.NEW_COMMENT IS DISTINCT FROM e.OLD_COMMENT)   AS comments_differ,
       COUNT_IF(e.NEW_REMARKS IS DISTINCT FROM e.OLD_REMARKS)   AS remarks_differ
FROM (SELECT MIN(OLD_UPDATED_DTTM) AS FIRST_V114_ROW
      FROM DAAS_PROD.DAAS_TEMP_WORK.DAASI3640_UPD_KEY
      WHERE OLD_REMARKS IS NOT NULL) t
LEFT JOIN DAAS_PROD.DAAS_TEMP_WORK.DAASI3640_UPD_KEY e
  ON e.OLD_UPDATED_DTTM >= t.FIRST_V114_ROW;


/* ---------------------------------------------------------------------
   S. THE SCOPE: which comps this run updates, and how many
   Nothing in the fact changes here either.
   --------------------------------------------------------------------- */

-- S1. The list. One row for every comp whose text differs from the rules and whose row in the
--     fact still reads what the key saw (a comp the load has rewritten since is left out: it is
--     right already). Texts are compared line by line, a line being what stands between two |
--     marks, so "$95" is not found inside "$95 BASED ON PLAY".
--       WRITE_REMARKS   the comp's remarks have a line the fact's remarks do not hold
--       WRITE_COMMENT   the comp's own comment has a line the fact's comment does not hold
--       IN_THIS_RUN     one of the two is true. A comp where neither is true gains nothing: the
--                       rule would only take text away from it, and it is left as it is.
--       TO_COMMENT, TO_REMARKS   what the row reads after the UPDATE. A column that is not
--                       written keeps today's value, so a comp that gets its remarks while it
--                       shows another comp's note keeps that note (S3 counts those).
--       SHOWS_LINES_NOT_ITS_OWN   the fact's comment has a line that the comp's own comment
--                       does not have: text the rule would take away.
--       WHAT            the kind of difference, for S3.
--     Use a Large.
CREATE OR REPLACE TRANSIENT TABLE DAAS_PROD.DAAS_TEMP_WORK.DAASI3640_UPD_SCOPE AS
WITH differ AS (        -- text differs from the rules, and the row still reads what the key saw
    SELECT k.COMP_DETAIL_FACT_SK, k.COMP_NBR, k.ISHDRW, k.PROPERTY_CD, k.CASINO_OUTLET_CD, k.GUEST_ID, k.ISSUE_DT,
           k.OLD_COMMENT, k.OLD_REMARKS, k.NEW_COMMENT, k.NEW_REMARKS
    FROM DAAS_PROD.DAAS_TEMP_WORK.DAASI3640_UPD_KEY k
    JOIN DAAS_PROD.DAAS_CORE.COMP_DETAIL_FACT f
      ON f.COMP_DETAIL_FACT_SK = k.COMP_DETAIL_FACT_SK
    WHERE k.WILL_CHANGE
      AND f.DELETE_IND = 'N'
      AND f.COMP_COMMENTS_DESC IS NOT DISTINCT FROM k.OLD_COMMENT
      AND f.COMMENTS_EXTENDED  IS NOT DISTINCT FROM k.OLD_REMARKS
),
own_comment_lines AS (  -- lines of the comp's own comment that the fact's comment does not hold
    SELECT d.COMP_DETAIL_FACT_SK, COUNT(*) AS LINES_MISSING
    FROM differ d, LATERAL FLATTEN(INPUT => SPLIT(d.NEW_COMMENT, '|')) x
    WHERE TRIM(x.VALUE::VARCHAR) <> ''
      AND POSITION('|' || x.VALUE::VARCHAR || '|' IN '|' || COALESCE(d.OLD_COMMENT, '') || '|') = 0
    GROUP BY d.COMP_DETAIL_FACT_SK
),
shown_comment_lines AS ( -- lines the fact's comment holds that are not in the comp's own comment
    SELECT d.COMP_DETAIL_FACT_SK, COUNT(*) AS NOT_ITS_OWN
    FROM differ d, LATERAL FLATTEN(INPUT => SPLIT(d.OLD_COMMENT, '|')) x
    WHERE TRIM(x.VALUE::VARCHAR) <> ''
      AND POSITION('|' || x.VALUE::VARCHAR || '|' IN '|' || COALESCE(d.NEW_COMMENT, '') || '|') = 0
    GROUP BY d.COMP_DETAIL_FACT_SK
),
remark_lines AS (       -- lines of the comp's remarks: not in the fact's remarks, and not said by the comment it shows
    SELECT d.COMP_DETAIL_FACT_SK,
           COUNT_IF(POSITION('|' || x.VALUE::VARCHAR || '|' IN '|' || COALESCE(d.OLD_REMARKS, '') || '|') = 0) AS LINES_MISSING,
           COUNT_IF(POSITION('|' || x.VALUE::VARCHAR || '|' IN '|' || COALESCE(d.OLD_COMMENT, '') || '|') = 0) AS NOT_IN_THE_COMMENT
    FROM differ d, LATERAL FLATTEN(INPUT => SPLIT(d.NEW_REMARKS, '|')) x
    WHERE TRIM(x.VALUE::VARCHAR) <> ''
    GROUP BY d.COMP_DETAIL_FACT_SK
),
marked AS (
    SELECT d.COMP_DETAIL_FACT_SK, d.COMP_NBR, d.ISHDRW, d.PROPERTY_CD, d.CASINO_OUTLET_CD, d.GUEST_ID, d.ISSUE_DT,
           d.OLD_COMMENT, d.OLD_REMARKS, d.NEW_COMMENT, d.NEW_REMARKS,
           COALESCE(c.LINES_MISSING, 0) > 0                                 AS WRITE_COMMENT,
           COALESCE(r.LINES_MISSING, 0) > 0                                 AS WRITE_REMARKS,
           COALESCE(r.NOT_IN_THE_COMMENT, 0) > 0                            AS REMARKS_SAY_MORE,
           COALESCE(o.NOT_ITS_OWN, 0) > 0                                   AS SHOWS_LINES_NOT_ITS_OWN,
           NULLIF(TRIM(REPLACE(d.NEW_COMMENT, '|', '')), '') IS NOT NULL    AS HAS_OWN_COMMENT
    FROM differ d
    LEFT JOIN own_comment_lines   c ON c.COMP_DETAIL_FACT_SK = d.COMP_DETAIL_FACT_SK
    LEFT JOIN shown_comment_lines o ON o.COMP_DETAIL_FACT_SK = d.COMP_DETAIL_FACT_SK
    LEFT JOIN remark_lines        r ON r.COMP_DETAIL_FACT_SK = d.COMP_DETAIL_FACT_SK
)
SELECT m.COMP_DETAIL_FACT_SK, m.COMP_NBR, m.ISHDRW, m.PROPERTY_CD, m.CASINO_OUTLET_CD, m.GUEST_ID, m.ISSUE_DT,
       m.OLD_COMMENT, m.OLD_REMARKS, m.NEW_COMMENT, m.NEW_REMARKS,
       m.WRITE_COMMENT, m.WRITE_REMARKS, m.SHOWS_LINES_NOT_ITS_OWN,
       IFF(m.WRITE_COMMENT, m.NEW_COMMENT, m.OLD_COMMENT) AS TO_COMMENT,
       IFF(m.WRITE_REMARKS, m.NEW_REMARKS, m.OLD_REMARKS) AS TO_REMARKS,
       (m.WRITE_COMMENT OR m.WRITE_REMARKS)
           -- AND m.ISSUE_DT >= '2025-01-01'    -- a floor on the issue date: only if one is wanted (S4 shows the years)
           AS IN_THIS_RUN,
       CASE WHEN m.WRITE_COMMENT AND m.SHOWS_LINES_NOT_ITS_OWN
                THEN '4. Comment missing, other text in its place: the comp''s own comment replaces it'
            WHEN m.WRITE_COMMENT
                THEN '3. Comment missing or incomplete: lines added'
            WHEN m.WRITE_REMARKS AND m.REMARKS_SAY_MORE
                THEN '1. Remarks missing: the report gains text'
            WHEN m.WRITE_REMARKS
                THEN '2. Remarks missing, same words as the comment: only the new column fills'
            WHEN m.SHOWS_LINES_NOT_ITS_OWN AND NOT m.HAS_OWN_COMMENT
                THEN '5. A note the rule does not give this comp: it would be blanked'
            WHEN m.SHOWS_LINES_NOT_ITS_OWN
                THEN '6. Lines the rule does not give this comp: they would be dropped'
            ELSE     '7. Other: nothing to add'
       END AS WHAT
FROM marked m;

-- S2. THE NUMBER. ROWS_THIS_RUN_UPDATES is what the UPDATE will report, and what 30b step 1
--     must show. Expect 1.2 to 1.3 million, with LEFT_AS_THEY_ARE near 6.6 million and
--     ALL_THAT_DIFFER near B3's COMPS_THAT_DIFFER.
--     Four things must hold or the UPDATE does not go ahead: COMMENTS_BLANKED is 0 (no row goes
--     from a comment to none), LONGEST_COMMENT is 1000 or less and LONGEST_REMARKS 4000 or less
--     (the column widths), and ROWS_WITHOUT_OWN_KEY is 0 (the UPDATE finds each row by
--     COMP_DETAIL_FACT_SK).
SELECT COUNT_IF(IN_THIS_RUN)                                                      AS rows_this_run_updates,
       COUNT_IF(NOT IN_THIS_RUN)                                                  AS left_as_they_are,
       COUNT(*)                                                                   AS all_that_differ,
       COUNT_IF(IN_THIS_RUN
                AND NULLIF(TRIM(REPLACE(OLD_COMMENT, '|', '')), '') IS NOT NULL
                AND NULLIF(TRIM(REPLACE(TO_COMMENT,  '|', '')), '') IS NULL)      AS comments_blanked,
       MAX(IFF(IN_THIS_RUN, LENGTH(TO_COMMENT), NULL))                            AS longest_comment,
       MAX(IFF(IN_THIS_RUN, LENGTH(TO_REMARKS), NULL))                            AS longest_remarks,
       COUNT(*) - COUNT(DISTINCT COMP_DETAIL_FACT_SK)                             AS rows_without_own_key
FROM DAAS_PROD.DAAS_TEMP_WORK.DAASI3640_UPD_SCOPE;

-- S3. What the number is made of, and what is left. Kinds 1 to 4 are this run: text that is
--     missing today. Kinds 5 to 7 gain nothing and are left as they are (7 is blank text against
--     no text, and the like). By the 10/29 count, 99.93% of the notes in kind 5 were written on
--     another comp that had the same number.
--     KEEP_LINES_THE_RULE_WOULD_REMOVE: comps of kinds 1 and 2 that get their remarks while the
--     comment they show stays, although the rule would take it away. They read "that note, then
--     the remarks" until the notes of kind 5 are dealt with.
--     Kind 2 changes nothing a reader of the report sees (the remark repeats the comment, and
--     the report shows a repeated line once). It is in so that the new column is complete.
SELECT WHAT,
       IFF(IN_THIS_RUN, 'yes', 'no')                                                    AS this_run,
       COUNT(*)                                                                         AS comps,
       COUNT_IF(IN_THIS_RUN AND NOT WRITE_COMMENT AND SHOWS_LINES_NOT_ITS_OWN)          AS keep_lines_the_rule_would_remove
FROM DAAS_PROD.DAAS_TEMP_WORK.DAASI3640_UPD_SCOPE
GROUP BY WHAT, IN_THIS_RUN
ORDER BY WHAT, this_run DESC;

-- S4. Optional: the same by year of issue, if a floor on the issue date is wanted. The floor is
--     the commented line in S1: take the dashes off, set the date, run S1 and S2 again.
SELECT YEAR(ISSUE_DT)                  AS issue_year,
       COUNT_IF(IN_THIS_RUN)           AS this_run_updates,
       COUNT_IF(NOT IN_THIS_RUN)       AS left_as_they_are
FROM DAAS_PROD.DAAS_TEMP_WORK.DAASI3640_UPD_SCOPE
GROUP BY 1
ORDER BY 1 DESC;

-- S5. Optional, a second opinion on the text before it is written, once the dynamic table has
--     refreshed since the deploy ("data_timestamp" later than "created_on" in the first
--     statement). The dynamic table is deployed code that builds the same two texts from raw by
--     itself, with no reference to the fact or to this list. Where this run writes a comment or
--     remarks, the dynamic table should already read the same: both DIFFER counts 0, or a
--     handful where raw has moved since its last refresh. NOT_ACTIVE_IN_DT counts comps the fact
--     holds active that CMS has deleted (the dynamic table applies the deletion, the fact has
--     not): they get their text like the rest and stay active. If this role cannot read the
--     dynamic table, Pete runs it.
SHOW DYNAMIC TABLES LIKE 'COMP_DETAIL_FACT_DT' IN SCHEMA DAAS_PROD.DAAS_CORE_GAMING;

SELECT COUNT(*)                                                             AS rows_this_run_updates,
       COUNT_IF(d.COMP_NBR IS NULL)                                         AS not_active_in_dt,
       COUNT_IF(d.COMP_NBR IS NOT NULL AND s.WRITE_COMMENT
                AND d.COMP_COMMENTS_DESC IS DISTINCT FROM s.TO_COMMENT)     AS comment_differs,
       COUNT_IF(d.COMP_NBR IS NOT NULL AND s.WRITE_REMARKS
                AND d.COMMENTS_EXTENDED  IS DISTINCT FROM s.TO_REMARKS)     AS remarks_differ
FROM DAAS_PROD.DAAS_TEMP_WORK.DAASI3640_UPD_SCOPE s
LEFT JOIN DAAS_PROD.DAAS_CORE_GAMING.COMP_DETAIL_FACT_DT d
  ON  d.COMP_NBR = s.COMP_NBR AND d.ISHDRW = s.ISHDRW AND d.PROPERTY_CD = s.PROPERTY_CD
  AND d.CASINO_OUTLET_CD = s.CASINO_OUTLET_CD AND d.DELETE_IND = 'N'
WHERE s.IN_THIS_RUN;


/* ---------------------------------------------------------------------
   The UPDATE and the emptying of the streams are in 30b, for the role
   that runs them. The UPDATE is repeated here for reference, commented
   out so that it cannot be run in passing from this file.
   --------------------------------------------------------------------- */
--  UPDATE DAAS_PROD.DAAS_CORE.COMP_DETAIL_FACT f
--  SET COMP_COMMENTS_DESC = s.TO_COMMENT,
--      COMMENTS_EXTENDED  = s.TO_REMARKS,
--      UPDATED_DTTM       = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,
--      UPDATED_BY         = CURRENT_USER,
--      LAST_DML_CD        = 'U'
--  FROM DAAS_PROD.DAAS_TEMP_WORK.DAASI3640_UPD_SCOPE s
--  WHERE f.COMP_DETAIL_FACT_SK = s.COMP_DETAIL_FACT_SK
--    AND s.IN_THIS_RUN
--    AND f.DELETE_IND = 'N'
--    AND f.COMP_COMMENTS_DESC IS NOT DISTINCT FROM s.OLD_COMMENT
--    AND f.COMMENTS_EXTENDED  IS NOT DISTINCT FROM s.OLD_REMARKS;


/* ---------------------------------------------------------------------
   C. AFTER (read-only). Run all of it before the load is resumed.
   --------------------------------------------------------------------- */

-- C1. Every comp of the run now reads what the list says. ROWS_THIS_RUN_UPDATES as in S2, and
--     the other three 0.
SELECT COUNT(*)                                                       AS rows_this_run_updates,
       COUNT_IF(f.COMP_DETAIL_FACT_SK IS NULL)                        AS row_not_found,
       COUNT_IF(f.COMP_COMMENTS_DESC IS DISTINCT FROM s.TO_COMMENT)   AS comment_wrong,
       COUNT_IF(f.COMMENTS_EXTENDED  IS DISTINCT FROM s.TO_REMARKS)   AS remarks_wrong
FROM DAAS_PROD.DAAS_TEMP_WORK.DAASI3640_UPD_SCOPE s
LEFT JOIN DAAS_PROD.DAAS_CORE.COMP_DETAIL_FACT f
  ON f.COMP_DETAIL_FACT_SK = s.COMP_DETAIL_FACT_SK
WHERE s.IN_THIS_RUN;

-- C2. Nothing else moved. The whole fact against the backup, over every column except the five
--     the UPDATE writes. Two rows with the same two numbers: not one other value changed, in any
--     row. Use a Large. (As DAAS_TEAM the masked employee columns read as their mask on both
--     sides. For those the proof is the UPDATE itself, which does not name them.)
SELECT '1. the fact now' AS what, COUNT(*) AS rows_,
       HASH_AGG(* EXCLUDE (COMP_COMMENTS_DESC, COMMENTS_EXTENDED, UPDATED_DTTM, UPDATED_BY, LAST_DML_CD)) AS every_other_column
FROM DAAS_PROD.DAAS_CORE.COMP_DETAIL_FACT
UNION ALL
SELECT '2. the backup', COUNT(*),
       HASH_AGG(* EXCLUDE (COMP_COMMENTS_DESC, COMMENTS_EXTENDED, UPDATED_DTTM, UPDATED_BY, LAST_DML_CD))
FROM DAAS_PROD.DAAS_TEMP_WORK.COMP_DETAIL_FACT_BKP_DAASI3640_UPD;

-- C3. The text moved only where it was meant to, and no comment was replaced with nothing. This
--     reads the fact against the backup, not the list: the first two numbers are equal, and
--     equal to ROWS_THIS_RUN_UPDATES, and COMMENTS_BLANKED is 0.
SELECT COUNT(*)                                                                    AS rows_whose_text_changed,
       COUNT_IF(s.IN_THIS_RUN)                                                     AS of_them_in_this_run,
       COUNT_IF(NULLIF(TRIM(REPLACE(b.COMP_COMMENTS_DESC, '|', '')), '') IS NOT NULL
                AND NULLIF(TRIM(REPLACE(f.COMP_COMMENTS_DESC, '|', '')), '') IS NULL) AS comments_blanked
FROM DAAS_PROD.DAAS_CORE.COMP_DETAIL_FACT f
JOIN DAAS_PROD.DAAS_TEMP_WORK.COMP_DETAIL_FACT_BKP_DAASI3640_UPD b
  ON b.COMP_DETAIL_FACT_SK = f.COMP_DETAIL_FACT_SK
LEFT JOIN DAAS_PROD.DAAS_TEMP_WORK.DAASI3640_UPD_SCOPE s
  ON s.COMP_DETAIL_FACT_SK = f.COMP_DETAIL_FACT_SK
WHERE f.COMP_COMMENTS_DESC IS DISTINCT FROM b.COMP_COMMENTS_DESC
   OR f.COMMENTS_EXTENDED  IS DISTINCT FROM b.COMMENTS_EXTENDED;

-- C4. The examples from the ticket. Tracy's two UTU comps: 7009616 reads "$95" with remarks
--     "$95 BASED ON PLAY|PER HUAIBI LI", and 4369229 reads "$80" with "$80 BASED ON LOSS 3/1|PER
--     HUAIBI LI". The merge case 7613391 (UTU, issued 2022-12-11) keeps its comment "TP". Her
--     five from 10/4 are not touched by this run: they read as they did before it (under the
--     full rule they would read blank and blank). Comment text can name people: not for the
